  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Saturday)\nIssued at 954 PM CST Sat Nov 21 2026\n\nZonal flow aloft will be short-lived at the beginning of the long\nterm period as an upper level trough begins to work its way \neastward into the Tennessee Valley by Tuesday night into Wednesday\nmorning, allowing increased rainfall chances (60-80%). \nFortunately, trends continue to be unsupportive of a high chance \nfor thunderstorm development as shear and instability remain low. \nUnfortunately, continued disagreement on the speed of the sfc low \nalong the Atlantic coast of Florida will largely dictate the exact\nrainfall amounts as well as timing. Therefore, continued with \nblended guidance for PoPs which has rainfall lingering through \nWednesday night before upper level ridging and sfc high pressure \nquickly filter in Thanksgiving morning. Thanksgiving and through \nthe weekend will bring much cooler conditions, with highs in the \n50s and overnight lows dropping into the upper 20s to lower 30s.\n\nBottom line: Wednesday will be a busy travel day ahead of the \nholiday and rainfall will likely affect commute plans. Be sure to \ncheck back in early next week as confidence increases in rainfall \ntotals and timing.",
